  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sky Wind Workshop",
    "overview": "A small wind-powered toy machine hangs above a painted cloud garden. Mint enamel rails, warm gold hardware, ivory letter tiles and six colored silhouettes make the mechanism feel manufactured, friendly and tangible. The center stays quiet enough to read the complete persistent row and its gold receiving cradle together.\n\nThe game uses real beveled meshes, a single orthographic view, live lettering and a separate illustrated backdrop. Compact platforms and visible joints establish the machine; soft buttons borrow its warm materials. This is the original, code-led P12 world chosen within the author's delegated direction. There is no approved composite image or user-research result to claim fidelity against.\n\nThis document records the implemented gameplay surface at P12. P13 event animation/audio and P14 full flow remain pending. The source of truth is `CascadeGame.cs`, `ToyMachineView.cs`, `ToyArt.cs`, `ShapeFaceGraphic.cs`, `ChevronGraphic.cs` and `ToyAssetBuilder.cs`; the relevant captures and layout measurements are in `Reports/P12`. Original-art and font provenance are recorded in `Docs/P12_ASSET_PROVENANCE.md`. Native glyph review, physical-device performance and human enjoyment remain unverified. Sidecar samples are flat, self-contained diagrams of the native components; synthesized color ramps are preview aids, not additional shipped palette values.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A calm painted sky surrounds a compact, fully visible toy machine.",
      "Six beveled silhouettes retain consistent color identity; live letters sit on ivory tiles.",
      "Thin mint platforms and gold joints give each floor a physical role.",
      "The stable gold receiver carries the complete destination below the floors.",
      "Warm rounded controls remain separate from the token bodies they operate."
